    "directions": [
      "Preheat the oven to 375°F (190°C) and line a muffin tin with paper liners.",
      "In a mixing bowl, whisk the flour, ½ cup (100 g) sugar, lemon zest, baking powder, salt and nutmeg. Stir in the melted butter and blend until the mixture is an even crumbly texture. Set aside.",
      "Measure ½ cup (75 g) of the flour mixture into a separate bowl and stir in the remaining 1 Tbsp (12 g) sugar and the cinnamon to make a streusel topping. Set aside.",
      "Add the milk, eggs and vanilla to the remaining flour mixture and whisk until smooth. Stir in the fresh and dried blueberries.",
      "Divide the batter between the muffin cups and sprinkle the tops with the streusel topping. Bake the muffins for about 25 minutes, until a toothpick inserted in the centre of one comes out clean. Cool the muffins in the tin for 10 minutes, then remove them from the tin to cool completely."
    ],
